## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model privacy-preserving analytics, not ML, with real-world trade-offs across storage, compute, energy, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy budgets & CRDTs for local aggregation
- Edge-resource constraints and telemetry design
- Compliance costs and regulatory penalties

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple CRDT-like Grow-Only Counter
class GCounter { constructor() { this.counters = new Map(); }
inc(k, v=1){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0)+v,0)); }
merge(other){ for(const [k,v] of other.counters){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0), v)); } }
value(){ let s=0; for(const v of this.counters.values()) s+=v; return s; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CRDT reconciliation when offline and merging after sync?
- What metrics would you track to detect drift in your aggregates and how would you price the analytics feature?

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges practical CBA skills for privacy-conscious features that touch user data, emphasizing cost modeling, data minimization, and risk assessment.

## Key Concepts
- On-device processing, data minimization, and opt-in consent
- Batch sizing, compression, and secure transmission
- Cost levers: storage, CPU energy, network, compliance, and hosting
- Go/no-go criteria tied to break-even and risk tolerance

## Code Example
```javascript
function batchEvents(events, batchSize) {
  const batches = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < events.length; i += batchSize) {
    batches.push(events.slice(i, i + batchSize));
  }
  return batches;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy risk post-implementation (DPIA outcomes, audits)?
- What metrics signal a need to adjust batch size or cadence?

