## Why This Is Asked

Balances privacy, regulatory needs, and system load by moving KYC attestation on-device.

### Key Concepts

- On-device cryptography and attestation
- Data minimization and privacy
- Key management and rotation
- Compliance and auditability

### Code Example

```javascript
async function signAttestation(privateKey, payload) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const data = enc.encode(JSON.stringify(payload));
  const sig = await crypto.subtle.sign({name: 'ECDSA', hash: 'SHA-256'}, privateKey, data);
  return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(sig)));
}
```

### Follow-up Questions

- How to handle key compromise and revocation?
- What metrics drive break-even and rollout schedule?
- How to prevent replay attacks and ensure forward secrecy?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical understanding of edge caching systems, cost modeling, and operational considerations for beginner-friendly distributed systems design.

## Key Concepts

- Edge caching strategies and TTL-based invalidation
- Delta synchronization for bandwidth optimization
- Energy-aware system design for battery-powered devices
- Phased rollout planning with cohort analysis
- Offline-first architecture and fallback behavior
- Privacy, compliance, and regulatory considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
function needsRefresh(lastRefresh, ttlHours) {
  const now = Date.now();
  const ttlMs = ttlHours * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  return (now - lastRefresh) >= ttlMs;
}

function getRefreshStrategy(device) {
  const batteryLevel = device.battery ?? 100;
  const isCharging = device.isCharging ?? false;

  if (batteryLevel < 20 && !isCharging) {
    return 'defer';
  } else if (batteryLevel < 50) {
    return 'adaptive';
  }
  return 'standard';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about client-side privacy, offline UX, and cost trade-offs without server trust. The candidate must specify concrete numbers, crypto choices, and go/no-go criteria, balancing performance, storage, and regulatory costs.

## Key Concepts

- Client-side encryption and key management
- Data growth and local cache sizing
- Delta synchronization vs full sync
- Privacy/compliance implications and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example using Web Crypto API AES-GCM
async function encrypt(plaintext, cryptoKey) {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    cryptoKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(plaintext)
  );
  return { encrypted, iv };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cost-benefit for privacy-preserving identity with ZK; evaluates crypto choices, on-device constraints, privacy, compliance, rollout, and measurement plans.

## Key Concepts

- Zero-knowledge proofs (ZK)
- On-device cryptography and secure enclaves
- Energy/perf trade-offs in mobile environments
- Data minimization and regulatory compliance
